    "title": "<p class=\"TableTitle\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Table&nbsp;10.03</span></strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\"> Overview of the most relevant prognostic and predictive markers in chronic lymphocytic leukaemia (CLL)</span></p>",
    "legend": "",
    "source": "Eichhorst Barbara (Taken from LYM5 4.3.1.3)",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "<table class=\"MsoNormalTable\" style=\"width: 25cm; border-collapse: collapse;\" border=\"0\" width=\"945\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"width: 141.7pt; border-right: none; border-bottom: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-top: 1pt solid black; background: #8db3e2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"189\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Parameter</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 5cm; border-right: none; border-bottom: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-top: 1pt solid black; background: #8db3e2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"189\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Frequency</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 5cm; border-right: none; border-bottom: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-top: 1pt solid black; background: #8db3e2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"189\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Prognostic impact</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 5cm; border-right: none; border-bottom: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-top: 1pt solid black; background: #8db3e2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"189\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Predictive impact</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 5cm; border-right: none; border-bottom: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-top: 1pt solid black; background: #8db3e2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"189\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Comment</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"width: 141.7pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"189\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">del(17p) and/or <em>TP53</em> mutation</span></strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\"> <strong>(~60% of cases carry both del(17p) and <em>TP53</em> mutation) </strong><span class=\"Ref-ID\" style=\"color: windowtext; border: none;\">{30442727}</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 5cm; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"189\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">del(17p) 4&ndash;8% and <em>TP53</em> mutation 5&ndash;12% in early-stage CLL <span class=\"Ref-ID\" style=\"color: windowtext; border: none;\">{30442727}</span></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">del(17p) 5&ndash;8% and <em>TP53</em> mutation 8&ndash;12% at start of first-line therapy <span class=\"Ref-ID\" style=\"color: windowtext; border: none;\">{20697090;24652989;31166681;30501481}</span></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">40&ndash;50% in relapsed and refractory CLL <span class=\"Ref-ID\" style=\"color: windowtext; border: none;\">{30442727}</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 5cm; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"189\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Strong negative prognostic impact on PFS and OS without therapy and with CIT, less adverse impact with targeted therapy (BTK and BCL2 inhibitors) <span class=\"Ref-ID\" style=\"color: windowtext; border: none;\">{24652989;30442727}</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 5cm; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"189\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Predictive for poor response and shorter response duration, PFS, and OS with CIT, as compared with longer response duration, PFS, and OS with BTK and BCL2 inhibitors <span class=\"Ref-ID\" style=\"color: windowtext; border: none;\">{30442727}</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 5cm; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"189\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Repeated testing at relapse is recommended</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Associated with a higher risk of RT</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"width: 141.7pt; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"189\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Complex karyotype: defined as &ge;&nbsp;3 or &ge;&nbsp;5 aberrations</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 5cm; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"189\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">15% detectable by chromosome banding analysis <span class=\"Ref-ID\" style=\"color: windowtext; border: none;\">{30602617}</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 5cm; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"189\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Independent negative prognostic impact in most studies, particularly for &ge;&nbsp;5 aberrations in <em>TP53</em>-wildtype cases <span class=\"Ref-ID\" style=\"color: windowtext; border: none;\">{30602617;31974198}</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 5cm; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"189\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Not clear, because the predictive impact is also dependent on involved chromosomal and genetic abnormalities; limited evidence from prospective trials</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 5cm; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"189\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Strong correlation with <em>TP53</em> aberrations, but still an independent prognostic factor</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">The optimal definition with respect to defining a number of chromosomal aberrations is unclear</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">The role of involved chromosomal and genetic abnormalities beyond <em>TP53</em> is to be evaluated <span class=\"Ref-ID\" style=\"color: windowtext; border: none;\">{30602617}</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"width: 141.7pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"189\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">IGHV status: U-CLL with &ge;&nbsp;98% identity vs M-CLL with &lt;&nbsp;98% identity</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 5cm; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"189\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">~30% U-IGHV in early-stage CLL <span class=\"Ref-ID\" style=\"color: windowtext; border: none;\">{32267500}</span></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">50&ndash;75% U-IGHV in advanced stages <span class=\"Ref-ID\" style=\"color: windowtext; border: none;\">{10477712;10477713;24652989}</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 5cm; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"189\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">U-IGHV: negative prognostic impact on PFS and OS without therapy and with CIT, less adverse impact with targeted therapy (BTK and BCL2 inhibitors) <span class=\"Ref-ID\" style=\"color: windowtext; border: none;\">{27185642;26486789;31628428;34709929}</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 5cm; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"189\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">U-IGHV: predictive for shorter response duration, PFS, and OS with CIT, as compared with longer response duration, PFS, and OS with BTK and BCL2 inhibitors</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 5cm; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"189\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">No repeated testing, because IGHV gene somatic hypermutation status does not change over time</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"width: 141.7pt; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"189\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><em><span lang=\"EN-GB\">BTK</span></em><span lang=\"EN-GB\"> mutation</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 5cm; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"189\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">None in BTK-inhibitor-treatment&ndash;na&iuml;ve patients <span class=\"Ref-ID\" style=\"color: windowtext; border: none;\">{25498455;29259203}</span>; 23&ndash;57% of relapsed CLLs on ibrutinib had <em>BTK</em> mutations after a median of 3&nbsp;years <span class=\"Ref-ID\" style=\"color: windowtext; border: none;\">{28366935;31243043}</span>; 60&ndash;80% of ibrutinib-resistant CLLs had <em>BTK</em> mutations, which were retrospectively detectable at a median of 8&ndash;9&nbsp;months (range: 3&ndash;18&nbsp;months) before clinical progression <span class=\"Ref-ID\" style=\"color: windowtext; border: none;\">{28049639;28418267;29259203}</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 5cm; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"189\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Not tested as an independent parameter</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 5cm; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"189\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Predictive for progression on therapy with covalent BTK inhibitors within the subsequent 3&ndash;18&nbsp;months <span class=\"Ref-ID\" style=\"color: windowtext; border: none;\">{28418267}</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 5cm; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"189\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">No routine testing so far</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"width: 141.7pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"189\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><em><span lang=\"EN-GB\">PLCG2</span></em><span lang=\"EN-GB\"> mutation</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 5cm; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"189\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">13% of relapsed CLLs after 3&nbsp;years on ibrutinib had <em>PLCG2</em> mutations in addition to <em>BTK</em> mutations <span class=\"Ref-ID\" style=\"color: windowtext; border: none;\">{31243043}</span></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">6% of ibrutinib-resistant CLLs had a sole <em>PLCG2</em> mutation, and 13% had <em>PLCG2</em> and <em>BTK</em> mutation <span class=\"Ref-ID\" style=\"color: windowtext; border: none;\">{28418267}</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 5cm; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"189\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Not tested as an independent parameter</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 5cm; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"189\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Predictive for progression on therapy with (covalent and non-covalent) BTK inhibitors <span class=\"Ref-ID\" style=\"color: windowtext; border: none;\">{28418267}</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 5cm; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"189\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">No routine testing so far</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"width: 141.7pt; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"189\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><em><span lang=\"EN-GB\">BCL2</span></em><span lang=\"EN-GB\"> mutation</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 5cm; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"189\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">45&ndash;47% of patients with venetoclax-resistant CLL have detectable <em>BCL2</em> mutations <span class=\"Ref-ID\" style=\"color: windowtext; border: none;\">{30514704;32232486}</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 5cm; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"189\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Not tested as an independent parameter</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 5cm; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"189\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Predictive for progression on venetoclax monotherapy <span class=\"Ref-ID\" style=\"color: windowtext; border: none;\">{30514704;32232486}</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 5cm; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"189\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">No routine testing so far</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"width: 141.7pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"189\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Serum B2M</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 5cm; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"189\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Elevated in 34% of patients with CLL <span class=\"Ref-ID\" style=\"color: windowtext; border: none;\">{27185642;30442727}</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 5cm; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"189\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lan